.TH IREE-ROCKET-BENCHMARK-MODULE 1 "November 2026" "iree-rocket" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iree-rocket-benchmark-module \- IREE's iree-benchmark-module with the Rocket NPU driver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iree-rocket-benchmark-module
.BI \-\-module= MODULE.vmfb
.BI \-\-function= NAME
.BR \-\-device=rocket " " \-\-device=local\-task
[\fB\-\-input=\fIINPUT\fR...]
[\fIOPTION\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
IREE's
.B iree-benchmark-module
built with the Rocket HAL driver for the RK3588 NPU linked in, and renamed so
it cannot collide with an upstream IREE installation. It times repeated calls
of one function of a .vmfb module, using Google Benchmark's options
(\fB\-\-benchmark_min_time\fR, \fB\-\-benchmark_repetitions\fR and so on).
.PP
Modules from
.BR rocket-compiler (1)
place their work on two devices, so pass both, in this order:
.B \-\-device=rocket \-\-device=local\-task
.PP
Run it with
.B \-\-help
for the full list of IREE's options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/accel/accel0
The NPU, through the mainline rocket kernel driver. Opening it needs read and
write access, which Debian gives the
.B render
group.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iree-rocket-run-module (1),
.BR rocket-run-module (1),
.BR rocket-compiler (1)
